## Fix 5 review issues on PR #2177 (branch: copilot/add-firestore-click-tracker)

The PR #2177 "feat: track affiliate clicks in Firestore" on branch `copilot/add-firestore-click-tracker` has 5 review issues to fix. Push the fixes as commits on that same branch so they appear in the existing PR.

### File 1: frontend/src/utils/firestoreClickTracker.ts

Two fixes needed:

**A) Replace Math.random() with crypto.randomUUID() (CodeQL insecure randomness)**

Current code in getAnonymousSessionId():
```typescript
const id = `anon_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 9)}`;
sessionStorage.setItem(key, id);
return id;
```

Replace with:
```typescript
const generateId = (): string => {
  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.crypto?.randomUUID) {
    return `anon_${window.crypto.randomUUID()}`;
  }
  return `anon_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 9)}`;
};

try {
  const existing = sessionStorage.getItem(key);
  if (existing) return existing;
  const id = generateId();
  sessionStorage.setItem(key, id);
  return id;
} catch {
  return generateId();
}
```

**B) Guard against uninitialized Firebase app**

Change import:
```typescript
import { getApps, getApp } from 'firebase/app';
```

Add at the start of the async IIFE inside trackClickToFirestore:
```typescript
if (!getApps().length) return;
```

### File 2: firestore.rules

Replace the click_events match block with a hardened version. Add helper functions inside the service block and update the match rule:

```
function isAllowedClickEventTerritory(territory) {
  return territory is string
         && ['GP', 'MQ', 'GF', 'RE', 'YT', 'guadeloupe', 'martinique', 'guyane', 'reunion', 'mayotte'].hasAny([territory]);
}

function isOptionalBoundedString(data, field, maxLen) {
  return !data.keys().hasAny([field])
         || (data[field] is string && data[field].size() > 0 && data[field].size() <= maxLen);
}

match /click_events/{docId} {
  allow create: if request.resource.data.keys().hasAll(['retailer', 'territory', 'price', 'clickedAt'])
                && request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(['retailer', 'territory', 'price', 'clickedAt', 'barcode', 'pageUrl', 'sessionId'])
                && request.resource.data.retailer is string
                && request.resource.data.retailer.size() > 0
                && request.resource.data.retailer.size() <= 100
                && isAllowedClickEventTerritory(request.resource.data.territory)
                && request.resource.data.price is number
                && request.resource.data.price >= 0
                && request.resource.data.price <= 10000
                && request.resource.data.clickedAt is timestamp
                && request.resource.data.clickedAt == request.time
                && isOptionalBoundedString(request.resource.data, 'barcode', 128)
                && isOptionalBoundedString(request.resource.data, 'pageUrl', 2048)
                && isOptionalBoundedString(request.resource.data, 'sessionId', 128);
  allow read: if false;
}
```

### File 3: frontend/src/utils/priceClickTracker.ts

Update the file header JSDoc comment. The current comment says "No external service — all data stays on the user's device" which is no longer accurate. Replace the header to mention that retailer clicks are also forwarded to Firestore anonymously (no PII: only retailer, barcode, territory, price, pathname, anonymous sessionId).

