The current single entry point (`overshoot`) re-exports both `StreamClient` (server-safe) and `RealtimeVision` (browser-only) from the same bundle. When Node.js imports `StreamClient`, the module evaluator also loads `RealtimeVision` which references `document.createElement`, causing:

  ReferenceError: document is not defined

This adds a separate `overshoot/server` entry point that exports only server-safe code (StreamClient, types, errors) without importing RealtimeVision or any browser-dependent modules.

Usage:
  // Node.js / server-side (NEW)
  import { StreamClient } from 'overshoot/server';

  // Browser (unchanged)
  import { RealtimeVision, StreamClient } from 'overshoot';

Changes:
- Add `src/server.ts` - server-safe exports (no RealtimeVision)
- Add `./server` to package.json `exports` map
- Add `src/server.ts` to tsup entry points

Daily Hexium previously gated submissions against exact slot matches, telling the player explicitly whether a word was right or wrong. This replaces that with a tile-destruction mechanic: any valid word destroys the tiles it used with a shatter animation, leaving the player to infer meaning from what remains. Win is detected when all tiles are gone; the intended solution is revealed only in the results modal.

## Changes

### `Hexium-state.js`
- Added `isAllTilesSpent(usedTileIds, allTiles)` — replaces `isSolved` as the daily win check

### `Hexium-app.js`
- `startDailyRound()`: passes `null` to `renderWordSlots` — hides the hint panel entirely
- `onSubmit()` daily path: removes slot-matching gate; accepts any valid word; triggers `destroyTiles()`; win fires via `isAllTilesSpent` inside the `onComplete` callback; toast shows score only (`+N` / `+N 🔥`, no `✓`)

### `Hexium-dom.js`
- `destroyTiles(tileIds, onComplete)`: adds `is-destroying` class, removes tile on `animationend`, calls `onComplete` when all are gone; handles `prefers-reduced-motion` by removing tiles synchronously
- `openResultsModal`: daily solved branch now renders a **"Today's solution:"** word list instead of the old slots-filled count

### `Hexium.css`
```css
@keyframes tile-shatter {
  0%   { transform: scale(1);    opacity: 1;   filter: brightness(1); }
  30%  { transform: scale(1.25); opacity: 0.9; filter: brightness(2) saturate(2); }
  100% { transform: scale(0);    opacity: 0;   filter: brightness(1); }
}
.hex-tile.is-destroying {
  animation: tile-shatter 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.6, 1) forwards;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 20;
}
```
Reduced-motion override collapses the animation to an instant `opacity: 0`.

### `Hexium.html`
- Added `#resultsSolutionList` div in the results modal for the solution reveal

